  "body": "host.js keeps a program a plugin starts off the host's stdin and stdout (`own` in `internal/plugin/host.js`): `\"inherit\"`, the fd number and `process.stdout`/`process.stdin` are mapped to stderr and to \"ignore\". `Bun.stdout` and `Bun.stdin` (BunFiles) are not caught, so `Bun.spawn({cmd: [...], stdout: Bun.stdout})` hands the child the host's real stdout.\n\nTwo effects:\n- What that program prints goes into the host's answers to magpie, the same corruption `own` exists to stop.\n- It keeps the host's stdout open after the host ends. Until the reaping fix for acezan's zombie report, that kept every such host `<defunct>` under magpie (reproduced on Linux with Bun 1.4.2: one more zombie per Restart). The reaping fix makes magpie wait for the host regardless, so this issue is only the protocol side now.\n\nFound while fixing the zombie report; left out of that change so it does one thing. Needs a check that `Bun.stdout === Bun.stdout` (or a fd comparison) in Bun 1.4.x, and a test in the host's spawn-guard tests.\n",
