   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T21:49:42Z",
   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5063-bun-standard-stream-guard), commit [09b8c0106](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/09b8c01069242d850c6689618e410f57e68d4bbc), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe existing child-process guard now recognizes the actual `Bun.stdin` and `Bun.stdout` objects, in both `Bun.spawn` and `Bun.spawnSync` argument forms and `stdio` arrays. Child stdin is closed and child stdout is directed to stderr; ordinary pipes and custom files keep their behavior.\n\nWith real Bun 1.4.4 and the embedded plugin host, eight child output lines corrupt RPC stdout on the base; after the fix all go to stderr and the next RPC succeeds. Parent focused checks passed under `-race`, as did plugin vet and the full `nogui` build. Full plugin-package race had a `TestPluginSOCKSProxy` HTTPS/dead-proxy failure; the same failure was reproduced with the original host predicate.\n\n`Bun.file(0)` and `Bun.file(1)` are different objects and are not covered by this identity check. No non-Linux runtime or full repository suite was tested. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
